---
import LabLayout from "../../layouts/LabLayout.astro";
---
<LabLayout
  title="Quantum Labs — hands-on sessions"
  description="Step-by-step quantum lab sessions. Stop reading, start doing — run the steps, hit the checkpoints, tick them off."
  currentSlug="labs"
  lang="en"
  altUrl="/hi/labs/"
  labSlug="labs-index"
>
  <section class="lab-hero">
    <div class="prompt">$ welcome to the lab</div>
    <h1>Quantum Labs</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Lessons teach you the ideas. <strong>Labs make you do them.</strong> Each lab is a step-by-step
      hands-on session: follow the steps, check your result against the checkpoints, and tick each
      step off as you go. Your progress is saved on this device.
    </p>
    <div class="lab-meta">
      <span class="lab-chip">step-by-step</span>
      <span class="lab-chip">checkpoints</span>
      <span class="lab-chip">your turn</span>
      <span class="lab-chip">debrief</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How a lab works</h2>
    <div class="how-grid">
      <div class="how-card">
        <span class="ic">🧪</span>
        <h3>Follow the steps</h3>
        <p>Numbered steps, one thing at a time. Tick the checkbox when a step is done.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="how-card">
        <span class="ic">🎯</span>
        <h3>Hit the checkpoints</h3>
        <p>Green boxes tell you exactly what you should see. If you don't see it — the amber box has your back.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="how-card">
        <span class="ic">✋</span>
        <h3>Your turn</h3>
        <p>Some steps hand you the controls: change one thing, predict, then run it and compare.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="how-card">
        <span class="ic">📓</span>
        <h3>Debrief</h3>
        <p>Every lab ends with what the experiment proved — and where the idea goes next.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Lab sessions</h2>
    <div class="lab-list">
      <a class="lab-card" href="/labs/lab-01-first-circuit/">
        <span class="lab-num">Lab 01 · ~45 min · beginner</span>
        <h3>Your first quantum circuit</h3>
        <p>Set up Python + Qiskit, build a real 1-qubit circuit, run it on a simulator — and watch superposition appear in the counts.</p>
      </a>
      <a class="lab-card" href="/labs/lab-02-quantum-gates/">
        <span class="lab-num">Lab 02 · ~40 min · beginner</span>
        <h3>Meet the quantum gates</h3>
        <p>Pauli, phase, and rotation gates on one qubit — then CNOT and your first entangled Bell pair on two.</p>
      </a>
      <div class="lab-card soon">
        <span class="lab-num">Lab 03</span>
        <h3>Next session — in the works</h3>
        <p>Stringing gates into real protocols. Dropping soon.</p>
        <span class="soon-tag">dropping soon</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What you'll need</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="font-size:16px">
      Lab 01 sets up Python and Qiskit on your machine (one time, about 15 minutes). Every lab after
      that builds on the same setup — no accounts, no cloud, no cost. If a lab ever needs anything extra,
      its first step will tell you exactly what to grab.
    </p>
  </section>
</LabLayout>
